{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"colourable-mystical-atlasmoth","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`rebar link-audit --repair` unconditionally aborts with \"a reconciler pass is in flight (refs/reconciler/lock held or unreadable) — refusing to repair\", even when no reconciler pass is running. The guard never reads the lock at all.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`link_audit._reconciler_in_flight` delegates to `fsck_repair._reconciler_in_flight` (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py:227`), which probes via:\n\n```\nfrom rebar_reconciler import _advisory_lock as advisory\n```\n\n`rebar_reconciler` is NOT importable from an in-process CLI invocation. It lives at `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler`, and `src/rebar/_engine` is deliberately not a package (no `__init__.py`) — the directory is put on PYTHONPATH by `engine_env`, which the CLI applies only when it shells out for the `reconcile` arm (`src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:148-160`). Every other arm runs without it.\n\nSo the import raises `ModuleNotFoundError`, the function takes its fail-CLOSED branch, and returns True regardless of the actual lock state. Verified directly:\n\n```\npython3 -c \"from rebar._commands.fsck_repair import _reconciler_in_flight; print(_reconciler_in_flight(\\\".\\\"))\"\nTrue\npython3 -c \"from rebar_reconciler import _advisory_lock\"\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \"rebar_reconciler\"\n```\n\nThe fail-closed policy itself is CORRECT — an indeterminate lock must not permit a destructive repair. The defect is that the probe is structurally unable to reach a determinate answer from the context it is called in, so \"indeterminate\" is the only outcome it can ever produce.\n\n## Impact\n\n- `link-audit --repair` (shipped in 9ad7-d5a2-a664-4827) is unusable. The 18 legacy bad edges in this repo tracker cannot be repaired, so story affe-2b42-4ee4-4e12 cannot meet its success criteria.\n- `fsck --repair` shares the same probe and the same import, so it is very likely affected identically. That path predates this work — needs confirming, and if so this is a latent pre-existing bug that link-audit merely surfaced.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe probe resolves the advisory module the way the engine does — put the engine directory on `sys.path` (or reuse `engine_env`) before importing — so it can genuinely distinguish \"lock held\" from \"cannot tell\". Fail-closed is retained for a genuinely unreadable lock; it must stop being the ONLY reachable outcome.\n\n## Notes\n\nDiscovered while running the authorized live repair for 9ad7-d5a2-a664-4827. Nothing was written: the tracker HEAD was unchanged and no `pre-link-audit-repair` tag was created, which confirms the abort happens before any mutation.","id":"480e-d9eb-7858-4e6d","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"link-audit --repair can never run: the reconciler in-flight probe fails closed on ImportError"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785385704505669001,"uuid":"236a8940-369f-4f0b-8379-91859b8812f4"}